From 572f14291a57e0e85768c6b5c72d2832778b67c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:12:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mp4, ts: Dolby Vision dual track / dual PID enhancement layer
 merged into the base layer

Profile 7 dual layer content with the enhancement layer (EL and RPU) in a
track or PID of its own is turned into the single track form: each EL access
unit is appended to the base layer access unit with the same DTS, every EL NAL
unit wrapped in a NAL unit of type 63 and the RPU (type 62) last.

MP4: an EL track (dvhe/dvh1 at a quarter of the base layer's size) gets no ES
(handled like a chapters track) and is read along with the base layer; its
hvcC parameter sets are added at IRAP pictures when the samples have none.
The presentation times are now computed from the decoding time before the edit
list clamping, which gave the first pictures of B-frame streams wrong (even
duplicate) times.

TS: the dependent PID comes from the full PMT (ts_psi.c; Ultra HD Blu-ray PMTs
span several packets): the Dolby Vision video stream descriptor without the
base layer, or HEVC 0x1015 next to 0x1011; the 3D MVC merging is reused with
the EL wrapped. Also for 3D MVC: a dependent PES is finished at a base PES
start only in .ssif files (elsewhere the next base AU may be interleaved with
it), the base PES wait in a queue of 8 for their dependent AUs, and the .ssif
seek read back searches the extents in steps smaller than an extent (the
exponential steps could skip a whole extent pair) and handles a position
inside a dependent view extent.

Message-Id: <20261012-dvfel-dovi-dual-layer-merge@djnice>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
